---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="The Practice — StillPoint" description="Everything that turns, turns around a point that holds still. Three small practices for finding yours — done out loud, in the open, with other people.">
  <!-- Page Header -->
  <header class="page-header">
    <div class="page-header-content">
      <p class="epigraph-coin">Find a third way.</p>
      <p class="epigraph">
        <em>A third way is almost never visible while you're being moved.</em><br>
        <em>This is where the standing still gets practiced — out loud, in the open, with other people.</em>
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <article class="practice-content">

    <!-- What a still point is -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>What a still point is</h2>

      <p>Everything that turns, turns around a point that holds still.</p>

      <p>You already know several. The top of a breath, before it turns. The beat in a room after somebody
      says something true and nobody rushes to fill it. The half-second between reading the message and
      starting to type.</p>

      <p>It isn't calm. Calm is a mood, and moods can't be scheduled. A still point is just a gap — small
      enough to fit inside five seconds, wide enough to stand in.</p>

      <p>It isn't made, either. It's found. It was in you before there was a coin at all.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Why the gap matters -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Why the gap is worth anything</h2>

      <p>When you're handed two options and both are wrong, the problem usually isn't that you chose badly.
      It's that the choice arrived already shaped, and you answered at the speed it was asked. Take it or
      leave it. Fight or fold. All in or all out. Whoever framed it that way got to keep the frame.</p>

      <p>The third option tends not to show up mid-swing. It shows up in the gap. That's the whole reason to
      practice making one — not to become serene, but to stop answering questions in the shape they were
      handed to you.</p>

      <p>None of this is new. Every culture that has ever existed found its own way here. Dervishes spinning
      until the spinning went still. Quakers sitting in silence until the light moved someone to speak. A
      farm kitchen gone quiet for grace. Not one tradition's property — closer to standard human equipment,
      arrived at independently, everywhere, for as long as there have been people.</p>

      <p>So nothing below is invented. It got crowded out, that's all; there is always something asking for
      the gap, and lately the things asking are very good at it. This is just the practice, written down
      plainly enough to keep.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- The practice itself -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>The practice itself</h2>

      <p>Three units, each one teachable in a breath.</p>

      <div class="practice-unit">
        <h3>The Still Point</h3>
        <p>Thumb on the touchstone — or any pebble, any worry bead, any object with some weight to it. One slow breath.
        Notice one real thing in the room: something you can name, something that's actually here. Five seconds.
        That's the whole practice. Every coin already teaches it; this is where it gets named.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="practice-unit">
        <h3>The Sit</h3>
        <p>Five minutes, once a day. No app, no streak counter, no check-in. You don't report to anything.
        This is the one wellness practice that never measures you — which is the point, and which is why it's
        harder than it sounds.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="practice-unit">
        <h3>The Still Hour</h3>
        <p>An hour together. Phones in a bowl. Something made by hand — bread, music, mending, anything that
        puts your body in the work. One round of "name one tension." No leader, no agenda past that, no
        permission needed to hold one. That paragraph is the whole format — you have everything you need
        to run one tonight.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Why we hold our own keys -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Why we hold our own keys</h2>

      <p>Every story of waking up — the cave, the dome, the endless feed — has the same structure: the
      operators offer two exits, and both exits are framed by the operators. The third way isn't picking
      a better exit. It's owning the ground you stand on.</p>

      <p>That's why this runs on software we host, coins we make ourselves, and materials anyone can fork.
      A room someone else owns can change the rules on you. This one can't.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- What this is -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>What this is</h2>

      <p>StillPoint began as a story — a novel about people relearning how to be still in a world built to
      keep them moving. From the start it was made in the open, as a collaboration between a human and AI,
      and it never pretended otherwise. In a project about finding a humane way to use these tools, hiding
      how it was made would have been the only real lie.</p>

      <p>The story was the proof. This is where the proof becomes a practice you can join.</p>

      <p>Not a pyramid — nothing here is trying to scale you, harvest you, or rank you. Something more like a
      tipi: small, portable, communal, yours to take down and carry whenever you're ready to go somewhere else.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- What you're not signing up for -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>What you're not signing up for</h2>

      <ul class="plain-list">
        <li>No guru. No one here has the answer you're supposed to follow.</li>
        <li>No hustle, no funnel, no growth target. Presence isn't a metric.</li>
        <li>No purity test. Skeptics, builders, and the unsure are all the right kind of person.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>This is small, and it's just beginning. That's the honest state of it.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Your first move -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Your first move</h2>

      <p>One thing, and it's not a task:</p>

      <p class="first-move"><strong>Come in, say who you are, and name one tension</strong> — the place <em>you</em> feel the pull between the pyramid
      and the tipi. Where the tools tempt you toward the extractive version, and where you'd rather build
      the humane one. No deliverable. Just honesty, out loud, where someone can meet it.</p>

      <p>That's how everyone starts. It's how we find each other.</p>

      <!-- WALLY: add your personal line here -->
    </section>

    <!-- Take the pattern -->
    <section class="section spore-block">
      <h2>Take the pattern</h2>

      <p>Take it. Run your own Still Hours, hand out your own coins, change what doesn't work. You don't
      need permission, and eventually you shouldn't need to come back here at all — the three practices
      above are short enough to carry in your head, which is the point of keeping them short.</p>

      <p>Movement materials here are shared under CC&nbsp;BY-SA, so anything that does get written down is
      yours to copy and adapt.</p>

      <p class="spore-note">No worksheet, no kit, no download. There isn't one yet, and the practice
      doesn't wait on it.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="cta-section">
      <p class="cta-label">Open the door</p>
      <a href="https://forum.stillpointproject.org" class="btn btn-primary" aria-label="Open the StillPoint forum">
        Open the door &rarr;
      </a>
      <p class="cta-note">
        This is early. One welcome post, one open room. The first few people in help shape what it becomes.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- License note -->
    <footer class="practice-footer">
      <p>
        StillPoint is a human–AI collaboration, made and run in the open.
        Movement materials are shared under
        <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" class="license-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>;
        the novel remains the author's — free to read, rights reserved.
        That's the whole arrangement, stated plainly.
      </p>
    </footer>

  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  @import '../styles/design-tokens.css';

  /* Page Header */
  .page-header {
    text-align: center;
    padding: var(--space-3xl) var(--space-lg) var(--space-2xl);
    max-width: var(--container-narrow);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .epigraph-coin {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    color: var(--color-accent-1);
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-lg);
    max-width: 52ch;
  }

  .epigraph {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2.5vw, 1.35rem);
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
    max-width: 52ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  /* Main Content */
  .practice-content {
    max-width: var(--container-narrow);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--space-lg) var(--space-3xl);
  }

  .section {
    max-width: 65ch;
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-2xl);
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
  }

  .section h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--font-size-2xl);
    color: var(--color-heading);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .section p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .section strong {
    color: inherit;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* Practice units */
  .practice-unit {
    margin: var(--space-xl) 0;
    padding-left: var(--space-lg);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .practice-unit h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    color: var(--color-accent-1);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm) 0;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .practice-unit p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  /* Spore block */
  .spore-block {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding-top: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .spore-block h2 {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xl);
  }

  .spore-note {
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
  }

  /* Plain list — no bullet gymnastics, just clear items */
  .plain-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: var(--space-md) 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .plain-list li {
    color: var(--color-text);
    padding: var(--space-sm) 0;
    padding-left: 1.5em;
    position: relative;
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
  }

  .plain-list li::before {
    content: '—';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--color-accent-1);
  }

  /* First move callout */
  .first-move {
    background: rgba(26, 42, 46, 0.6);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent-2);
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;
    margin: var(--space-lg) 0;
  }

  /* CTA */
  .cta-section {
    max-width: 65ch;
    margin: var(--space-xl) auto var(--space-2xl);
    text-align: center;
    padding: var(--space-2xl);
    background: linear-gradient(
      135deg,
      var(--color-bg-accent) 0%,
      rgba(147, 102, 57, 0.1) 100%
    );
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 10px;
  }

  .cta-label {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .cta-note {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .cta-note code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85em;
    color: var(--color-accent-2);
  }

  .btn {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: var(--space-md) var(--space-xl);
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: var(--font-size-base);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: all var(--transition-normal);
    cursor: pointer;
    border: none;
  }

  .btn-primary {
    background: var(--color-accent-1);
    color: var(--color-bg-accent);
  }

  .btn-primary:hover {
    background: var(--color-accent-2);
    color: var(--color-heading);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg);
  }

  /* Footer note */
  .practice-footer {
    max-width: 65ch;
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-xl);
    padding-top: var(--space-xl);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .practice-footer p {
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed);
  }

  .license-link {
    color: var(--color-accent-2);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .license-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* Mobile */
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .epigraph {
      font-size: 1.05rem;
    }

    .section h2 {
      font-size: var(--font-size-xl);
    }

    .practice-content {
      padding: 0 var(--space-md) var(--space-2xl);
    }

    .cta-section {
      padding: var(--space-lg);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .epigraph {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .btn {
      width: 100%;
      text-align: center;
    }
  }
</style>
